# Line endings matter here, not just cosmetically:
#
#   * cmd.exe mis-parses a .bat file that uses bare LF line endings, and a UTF-8
#     BOM makes it choke on the very first command.  run.bat must therefore stay
#     CRLF, so force it regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf setting.
#   * the example shell scripts must stay LF, or they fail under bash.
#
# The .bat is also kept ASCII-only outside its `echo` lines (see the test in
# tests/test_run_and_report.py): cmd parses command lines in the OEM codepage, so
# non-ASCII there gets mis-decoded and executed as garbage.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
